infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Performance as a loop vs as a project
  desc The same fix — kept alive by discipline, or quietly undone within six months
  compares
    - label Loop · a discipline
      children
        - label 5–10% of engineering time
          desc Steady cost, frontloaded into CI gates and observability
        - label Steady metrics year over year
          desc Each regression class is caught before it ships
        - label Fix half-life: indefinite
          desc A CI gate fails any PR that reintroduces the regression
    - label Project · a one-time fix
      children
        - label 20–40% of time in crisis mode
          desc Cost deferred to incident response, paid in firefights
        - label Crisis every 6–18 months
          desc Accumulated bytes, queries, and allocations undo the gain
        - label Fix half-life: 3–6 months
          desc New features drift performance back to the pre-fix level
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
